                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "seanzhangseu",
                        "email": "xiazhang@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "seanzhangseu"
                    },
                    "message": "@rashidmp@ami.com Did you verify if gateway of IPv4 kept after disable DHCPv4? The IP address was kept but the gateway was set to 0.0.0.0 after disabling DHCPv4."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "seanzhangseu",
                        "email": "xiazhang@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "seanzhangseu"
                    },
                    "message": "The BMC can not be accessed with the persist IPv4 address if gateway reset to 0.0.0.0"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "rashidmp",
                        "email": "rashidmp@ami.com",
                        "username": "rashidmp2002"
                    },
                    "message": "When switching from DHCP to static via Redfish, bmcweb explicitly clears the gateway. Fixing the gateway persistence needs to be done in bmcweb. I am working on that separately."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "seanzhangseu",
                        "email": "xiazhang@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "seanzhangseu"
                    },
                    "message": "Because for previous behavior, when disabling DHCP without static IP address, no IP addresses is expected. REF: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/70577\nBut the behavior changed with this commit, it's better to align with bmcweb for this behavior change according to my understanding.\nCan you help confirm? @johnathanx.mantey@intel.com Thanks."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "rashidmp",
                        "email": "rashidmp@ami.com",
                        "username": "rashidmp2002"
                    },
                    "message": "Reverted : https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-networkd/+/91813"
                }
